SUMMARY:Community Garden Open House
DESCRIPTION:Join NEEC on Saturday\, April 18\, 10-12\, at our Community Garden Open House! \nWhether you are an experienced gardener or just getting started\, this event offers an excellent opportunity to discover more about sustainable gardening and community engagement.\n*The importance of Community Gardens and Urban Farming\n*Bio-Intensive Agriculture\n*Compost\, compost tea\, and the Montclair Composting Program\n*Early spring crops and tips for maximizing garden productivity\n*Native plants\, wildlife habitats\, and pollinator gardens\n*How to bring sustainable gardening practices home \nEnjoy free parking\, as available\, at the Our Lady of Mt. Carmel Church (near the statue of the Virgin Mary) or on the street. Admission is free for all attendees.\nFor additional information\, please contact us at: Info@neearth.org \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
