SUMMARY:Celebrate Earth Day at Laurelwood Arboretum
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a free\, family-friendly Earth Day celebration at Laurelwood Arboretum on Saturday\, April 18\, from 12:00 PM to 4:00 PM. This popular annual event offers something for everyone\, including nature crafts\, bird walks\, scavenger hunts\, storytime\, and educational talks. Enjoy guided tours of the arboretum from 1:00 PM to 3:00 PM\, a perfect way to explore Laurelwood’s spring blooms and learn more about its diverse plantings and natural features. \nThe celebration will be held rain or shine at 725 Pines Lake Drive West in Wayne. Free shuttle service will run from 12:00 PM to 4:00 PM between the arboretum and the Pines Lake School parking lot\, located at 511 Pines Lake Drive. \nThe 2026 Earth Day theme\, “Our Power\, Our Planet\,” highlights the importance of community-based solutions\, clean energy\, and collective action to protect our environment.\nThis event is hosted by Friends of Laurelwood Arboretum and generously sponsored by Canete Landscaping and Garden Center of Wayne\, Glenwild Garden Center & Nursery of Bloomingdale and The Backyard Birding Store in Wayne. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/celebrate-earth-day-at-laurelwood-arboretum/
LOCATION:Laurelwood Arboretum\, 725 Pines Lake Drive West\, Wayne\, NJ
CATEGORIES:Kids & Families
