SUMMARY:TWO BY TWO at 2PM - Free staged reading of a new play
DESCRIPTION:TWO BY TWO AT 2pm\nSHORT PLAYS BY JOSEPH VITALE AND STEPHANIE GRIFFIN\nDiscussion with the author and audience follows the script-in-hand staged readings at the Cranford Community Center’s fully accessible 110-seat theater. Large print play programs / scripts upon advance request. A library staff member is present to help assist anyone in need of special accommodations.\nEdifice Wrecks by Stephanie Griffin – A hilarious and soaking-wet take on power\, propaganda\, and the danger of believing your own hype. Griffin\, a member of The Dramatists Guild\, holds a master’s degree in social work and has pursued careers as a teacher in a suburban high school and as a producer and video editor for television networks\, including NBC. An award-winning playwright and screenwriter\, she has staged her works with The Theater Project\, New Jersey Repertory Theatre\, and Free Fringe Philly\, among others.\nThe Cleaners by Joseph Vitale – Two night-shift cleaners find a torn-up love note and realize it might be their shot to cash in on a world that has never seen them. Vitale is the author of several plays that have been produced in theaters throughout the country. His last full-length play\, The Interpreter\, was produced by The Theater Project in 2024. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/two-by-two-at-2pm-free-staged-reading-of-a-new-play/
