SUMMARY:Heidi Gallery Free Performance: West African Drum\, Dance & Song
DESCRIPTION:West African Drum\, Dance & Song with Lara Gonzalez and Special Guest Artist\, Master Drummer\, Sanga-Of-The-Valley and special guest dancers from Passaic County Technical Institute\nSunday\, April 19\, 2026\, 2pm – 4pm\nGallery Open until 5pm \nExperience an interactive exploration of beautiful healing rhythms\, dances and songs from West Africa and beyond. \nJoin Lara Gonzalez\, Artistic Director and founder of Marafanyi Drum\, Dance & Song and her mentor and teacher\, Sanga-Of-The-Valley\, as they guide audience members through content including traditional music\, dance\, language and the introduction to indigenous instruments. \nTheir holistic approach to music and dance is fun\, encouraging and accessible to people of all abilities. Attendees are encouraged to bring their own shakers and light percussion instruments. \nPlease RSVP by 4/17/2026. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
